$HOME/BMH-OS/BMH Training Course/Thinkific/transcripts/changes/SLOT-02-terms-glossary.md:177:In CRM context, disposition means the outcome you record after a call. [curious] This is different from the disposition manager role we talked about earlier. After every call you make, you need to record a disposition in REsimpli. Examples include not interested, no answer, callback scheduled, appointment set, do not call, and wrong number. Accurate dispositions keep the pipeline clean and make sure the right leads get the right attention. You support the acquisition manager by finding and qualifying motivated sellers. [thoughtful] REsimpli is the hub for everything. Keep lead statuses and dispositions accurate after every call. Follow-up is where deals are made. And your KPIs are the scorecard that helps everyone, including you, get better over time.
